                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15056045" author="yzhdanov" created="Mon, 14 Dec 2015 14:34:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Raul, can you please take a look at this?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15060221" author="raulvk" created="Wed, 16 Dec 2015 16:07:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This module generates no binaries. The module is of type pom. It just contains resources which are attached to the build (the features descriptor).&lt;br/&gt;
It would be nice to include the latter inside the fabric package.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Regards,&lt;br/&gt;
Ra&#250;l.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15061874" author="yzhdanov" created="Thu, 17 Dec 2015 10:41:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Raul,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can you please add some kind of description on what exactly should be added and then assign this ticket to Anton Vinogradov - he knows everything on Ignite builds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15062044" author="raulvk" created="Thu, 17 Dec 2015 13:45:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hey,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You should add the generated features.xml (in the target directory, after the build has run) to this folder.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Regards,&lt;br/&gt;
Ra&#250;l.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15062145" author="skozlov" created="Thu, 17 Dec 2015 14:54:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I know but I still see no resources in ignite-osgi-karaf module. As I see for maven upload it should be a xml placed there?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15062180" author="avinogradov" created="Thu, 17 Dec 2015 15:21:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Raul,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m not familiar with OSGi, could you please make some more tips about my task?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15068126" author="raulvk" created="Tue, 22 Dec 2015 13:40:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don&apos;t need to be familiar with OSGi. &lt;br/&gt;
This module simply contains an XML file with placeholders that are replaced by Maven Resource Filtering.&lt;br/&gt;
You just need to copy the file: &lt;tt&gt;target/classes/features.xml&lt;/tt&gt; into the fabric assembly module.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Regards,&lt;br/&gt;
Ra&#250;l.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15068164" author="avinogradov" created="Tue, 22 Dec 2015 14:15:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Done, &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please check&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15068671" author="skozlov" created="Tue, 22 Dec 2015 20:19:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;As reporter I assigned the issue to myself&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
